y &= r \sin \theta = 8 \sin^2 \theta = 4 - 4 \cos 2 \theta.
\end{align*}Hence,
\[x^2 + (y - 4)^2 = 16 \sin^2 2 \theta + 16 \cos^2 2 \theta = 16.\]Thus, the graph of $r = 8 \sin \theta$ is the circle centered at $(0,4)$ with radius 4.

